{
  "hypotheses": [
    {
      "id": "h200-attn-20261020-01",
      "parents": [],
      "operation": "generate",
      "statement": "Share FlashMLA decode plans across compatible KV-cache groups within one metadata-building pass, conditional on the pinned H200 runner still creating duplicate plans. The supplied patch implements per-pass holder sharing; the author reports fewer planner launches on H20 TP8, using synthetic acceptance for serving measurements. That establishes an implementation mechanism, not an H200 benefit. Unlike small-head kernels, this change does not require TP4 or TP8 and can plausibly apply to TP1. Its value depends on exposed redundant planner work under real DSpark rejection. Reuse must preserve equal live lengths, masks and replay state, rather than merely matching tensor shapes. First inspect baseline membership and builder dispatch; then compare unchanged execution with sharing alone, preserving all serving settings and measuring primary-workload latency and throughput.",
      "observed_bottleneck": "No H200 bottleneck is measured. Supplied installed code shows same-type plan reuse but does not establish whether cross-group sharing already exists. The #58818 author reports 21 versus four planner launches per step on eight H20 GPUs at TP8/EP8; those counts cannot be assumed for TP1/DP4. H200 exposed planner time and effect size are unknown.",
      "mechanism": "Implementation evidence: #58818 creates a dictionary local to build_attn_metadata and shares holders keyed by block size, causality and decode SWA width. Transfer inference: eliminating repeated compatible planner launches can shorten decode's critical path without changing attention arithmetic. The improvement disappears if planning is already shared, groups are incompatible, or removed work is not exposed.",
      "proposed_change": "First inspect the pinned runner and all three affected files for equivalent sharing and actual builder use. If absent and eligible, port the per-pass dictionary and holder reuse. Preserve separate target, drafter and microbatch passes; retain per-group behavior when compatibility cannot be established.",
      "code_surface": "vllm/v1/attention/backend.py: CommonAttentionMetadata; vllm/v1/worker/gpu/attn_utils.py: build_attn_metadata; vllm/v1/attention/backends/mla/sparse_swa.py: metadata builder and tile-scheduler holders. Supplied #58818 patch commit: 0457e961490be6234aac531a76e40859874f9813.",
      "applicability": "Plausible SM90 transfer independent of small local attention-head counts. Qualification is deferred pending baseline membership, active runner, compatible group composition and graph-replay correctness. V1 callers without the dictionary and separately built drafter metadata do not automatically benefit. The source performance setup differs in topology, model revision, prefix caching, Engram placement and speculative acceptance.",
      "predicted_direction": "Conditionally lower decode TPOT and improve output throughput; little direct prefill benefit is expected. Magnitude, TTFT-tail effects and saturation benefit are unknown.",
      "classification": "upstream_port",
      "alternatives": [
        {
          "explanation": "The baseline already shares plans, or only one compatible group executes.",
          "distinguishing_test": "Inspect holder identity and lifetime, then count planner launches per eligible metadata pass and layer type. Already-shared execution has no incremental delta."
        },
        {
          "explanation": "Serving variation comes from rejection outcomes, rank skew or host scheduling rather than planning.",
          "distinguishing_test": "Use matched full runs with real rejection; separately replay matched batch metadata to measure planner removal. Join all-rank acceptance, scheduling and planner counters without treating profiled timing as serving performance."
        }
      ],
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source_id": "github:vllm-project/vllm:58818:patch",
          "quote": "cross_group_cache=cross_group_cache,",
          "relation": "supports"
        },
        {
          "source_id": "github:vllm-project/vllm:58818:patch",
          "quote": "FlashMLA checks only shapes",
          "relation": "challenges"
        },
        {
          "source_id": "github:vllm-project/vllm:58818:live-page",
          "quote": "Planner launches per decode step drop from 21 to 4.",
          "relation": "supports"
        },
        {
          "source_id": "code:h200-excerpts:attention",
          "quote": "out[layer_type] = get_mla_metadata()[0]",
          "relation": "context"
        }
      ],
      "novelty": {
        "scientific": "Existing redundant-work elimination; no scientific novelty claimed.",
        "implementation": "Port or activate existing cross-group plan sharing on the pinned serving branch.",
        "workload": "Evaluate TP1/DP4 with real DSpark rejection and native prefix traffic, rather than importing TP8 synthetic-acceptance results.",
        "nearest_prior_art": "vLLM #58818; existing same-type layer plan reuse.",
        "specific_delta": "Extend reuse from layers within a group to compatible groups within one pass, only if absent."
      },
      "prior_art_query": "FlashMLA cross-group plan reuse",
      "experiment": {
        "control": "The supplied pinned H200 baseline, including existing same-type reuse, seq64, graphcap512, native rejection and enabled telemetry. This existing static implementation is the primary comparator; no cheaper equivalent flag is established by the supplied sources.",
        "treatment": "First perform the source/configuration presence check. Then attest the port, verify activation and correctness, run an unprofiled screen, collect a separate mechanism diagnostic, and confirm with at least five alternating paired full-run blocks for small gains. Preserve native agent-f75 8K/1K prefixes and fixed-schedule Mooncake anchors adapted to seq64. Keep 1K/1K diagnostics separate.",
        "metrics": "Activation: shared-holder uses divided by compatible group/layer-type opportunities, plus planner launches per eligible pass, separately for target/drafter and eager/graph execution on every rank. Serving: request TPOT=(last-first token time)/(server output tokens-1), excluding undefined one-token cases; TTFT tails, exact output tokens, throughput, historical-scorer goodput and replay lag. Record all-rank draft/verify/accepted deltas, KV blocks, preemption, missing coverage and resets. Measure exposed planner time only in separate diagnostics.",
        "supports_if": "Compatible groups demonstrably share holders, redundant launches decrease, correctness passes, and paired full-run intervals show a predeclared useful TPOT or goodput improvement without unacceptable TTFT-tail or quality regression. Check baseline drift and use full runs as statistical units.",
        "rejects_if": "Equivalent sharing is already active; adequately covered execution has no redundant compatible plans; reuse violates live-value invariants; or adequately powered confirmation rules out the predeclared useful serving improvement.",
        "inconclusive_if": "Runner dispatch, eligible opportunities or telemetry coverage are unresolved; intervals overlap both useful improvement and regression; or source-level launch removal cannot be connected to exposed execution time. Sparse or uncovered zero-hit counts are inconclusive.",
        "held_out_condition": "Ragged arrivals, mixed prefill/decode, cold and warm prefixes, long contexts, idle DP ranks and changing speculative outcomes, using the same seq64 topology.",
        "correctness": "Exercise the newly shared-cache branch explicitly. Check equal live topk_length, extra_topk_length, masks and replay state across participating groups; prevent reuse across unrelated passes. Compare eager and graph replay after changing lengths, page tables, padding and request membership. Verify plan refresh, separate target/drafter ownership, output equivalence and distributed isolation. Map these checks to applicable G01-G05 once their definitions are supplied.",
        "cost": "Low relative integration effort: three Python files and no kernel rebuild indicated by the supplied patch; actual port effort remains unknown. Stop after the presence check if redundant planning is absent. With eight-GPU node price P per hour, report cost per output token as P*T/(3600*N_output); P is unknown. Exclude profiling runs from the serving frontier."
      },
      "revision_reason": "Initial proposal incorporates the shape-only validation objection by requiring live-value equality and explicit shared-branch replay tests."
    },
    {
      "id": "h200-attn-20261020-02",
      "parents": [],
      "operation": "generate",
      "statement": "Test direct paged candidate-only indexer scoring as a conditional replacement for dense scoring followed by masking in consumer layers. The supplied #62463 patch describes reading candidate K in place and retaining device-resident live lengths; #62000 instead gathers K before scoring. These are competing implementations of the same work-elimination mechanism, not cumulative optimizations. H20 evidence is conflicting: gathering regressed at one request, while direct scoring's lower ITL came from tiny samples and did not consistently improve throughput. The transfer hypothesis is that avoiding both discarded scoring and intermediate K copies helps eligible H200 long-context decode. First establish actual indexer shapes, cache format and baseline dispatch. Keep dense scoring as the short-context comparator and default; require native 8K/1K evidence before claiming a useful change to this deployment.",
      "observed_bottleneck": "No H200 scoring bottleneck is measured. #62000 reports profiler-derived improvements at approximately 1M context and nine requests on H20 TP8, but an approximately 11.6% single-request regression. #62463 reports lower mean ITL on H20 TP8 with 1,029,974 input and 16,384 output tokens, using only one run per arm and 2/4/8/16 requests at C1/2/4/8. At C4, overall completion throughput fell 1.5%. Its profiling batches also differed. These are author-reported results, not independently verified H200 observations.",
      "mechanism": "Implementation evidence: #62463 exposes direct paged candidate scoring with compact logits and device-side causal-bound preparation; #62000 exposes candidate-K gathering and default-off controls. Both avoid full compressed-context scoring for consumers. Transfer inference: direct reads may additionally avoid gather workspace traffic and fixed copy cost. Benefits depend on actual indexer shapes and context-to-candidate width, not TP-local attention-head padding.",
      "proposed_change": "First inspect complete installed call sites, patch integration, FP8 indexer-cache layout, context-parallel configuration and actual consumer dispatch. If eligible and absent, adapt #62463 to the pinned branch while preserving live device inputs and configuration-based graph selection. Keep dense scoring available. Evaluate #62000 as a separate mutually exclusive comparator; do not stack the implementations or infer a profitable H200 threshold from its example settings.",
      "code_surface": "vllm/model_executor/kernels/attention/dsa/candidate_paged_logits.py; sparse_attn_indexer.py; vllm/v1/attention/backends/mla/indexer.py; vllm/envs.py; tests/kernels/attention/test_candidate_paged_logits.py. Alternative arm: candidate_gather.py and its supplied integration paths. The supplied patch excerpts do not include complete scoring and dispatch bodies.",
      "applicability": "Deferred long-context candidate. Target H200 is SM90, but FP8 attention KV settings alone do not prove indexer-cache eligibility. Confirm actual indexer heads, strides, candidate widths, causal metadata and architecture gates. TP1's 64 attention heads neither prove nor disprove indexer-kernel compatibility. Candidate-source layers, pre-candidate layers and prefill remain outside the proposed change. Model accuracy, short-workload safety and H200 effect size are unknown.",
      "predicted_direction": "Potentially lower consumer-indexer time and long-context TPOT, especially when dense scoring scans substantially more positions than the candidate set. Short-context or low-row regressions remain plausible. No capacity, general throughput or primary-workload improvement is established.",
      "classification": "adaptation",
      "alternatives": [
        {
          "explanation": "Dense scoring wins on H200 because short contexts, few rows or TP1 indexer shapes make candidate bookkeeping more expensive than discarded scoring.",
          "distinguishing_test": "Compare dense, gather and direct paged scoring on identical captured inputs across observed row counts and compressed lengths, including one request and the native 8K/1K workload. Include every preparation, scoring, top-k and remap stage."
        },
        {
          "explanation": "Lower client ITL reflects acceptance, streaming chunks, prefix-cache state or batch composition rather than a faster serving path.",
          "distinguishing_test": "Measure server-token-based request TPOT and whole-run completion goodput; record exact tokens, rank-local prefix hits and all-rank acceptance counters. Use matched-shape diagnostics separately to attribute kernel work."
        },
        {
          "explanation": "Any benefit comes mainly from top-k operating on fewer logits, rather than direct scoring or avoided K copies.",
          "distinguishing_test": "Keep the selector backend fixed across arms and time preparation, scoring, selection and remapping separately at identical shapes. Compare gather and direct scoring using the same candidate set and compact width."
        }
      ],
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source_id": "github:vllm-project/vllm:62463:patch",
          "quote": "No per-step host decision.",
          "relation": "supports"
        },
        {
          "source_id": "github:vllm-project/vllm:62000:patch",
          "quote": "without requantizing K.",
          "relation": "supports"
        },
        {
          "source_id": "github:vllm-project/vllm:62000:live-page",
          "quote": "11.6% slower",
          "relation": "challenges"
        },
        {
          "source_id": "github:vllm-project/vllm:62463:live-page",
          "quote": "This is one A/B pair, not a confidence-interval result.",
          "relation": "challenges"
        },
        {
          "source_id": "github:vllm-project/vllm:62463:live-page",
          "quote": "Accuracy and shorter-workload checks are still pending.",
          "relation": "challenges"
        }
      ],
      "novelty": {
        "scientific": "Existing candidate-restricted scoring; no new algorithm claimed.",
        "implementation": "Adapt an explicit SM90 implementation to the pinned TP1 deployment and validate graph-live inputs.",
        "workload": "Resolve conflicting low-concurrency evidence and test whether long-context benefits survive native prefix traffic and H200 seq64 execution.",
        "nearest_prior_art": "vLLM #62463 direct paged scoring and #62000 gather-based scoring, both addressing #61830.",
        "specific_delta": "Replace consumer dense-score-then-mask execution with direct candidate scoring, conditional on eligibility; retain dense execution where the alternative lacks serving value."
      },
      "prior_art_query": "candidate-only paged indexer scoring",
      "experiment": {
        "control": "Pinned baseline dense scoring plus candidate masking and the unchanged deployed top-k backend. Use three mutually exclusive static arms: dense with both candidate flags off; #62000 gather only; #62463 direct paged only. Dense is the strongest simple short-context comparator. Calibrate and freeze any gather workload gates before held-out evaluation; FORCE is for validation, not a production policy.",
        "treatment": "Start with source/configuration membership and eligibility checks. After activation and correctness, screen each arm unprofiled on native agent-f75 and fixed-schedule Mooncake at seq64, then run separate long-context and cache-isolated diagnostics. Compare surviving arms in at least five alternating paired full-run blocks for small gains. Keep topology, speculation, prefixes, logging and scheduler settings fixed. Do not add a host context-length branch inside captured execution; any future mixed-workload routing requires separate graph-safe qualification.",
        "metrics": "Activation: candidate-path consumer calls and rows divided by all structurally eligible consumer calls and rows, stratified by live compressed length, row count, eager/graph mode and rank. Record fallback reasons and whether consumer mask kernels disappear. Measure request TPOT using exact server output tokens, TTFT tails, throughput, historical-scorer goodput, replay lag, all-rank draft/verify/accepted deltas, prefix hits, KV blocks, preemption and workspace high-water marks. Separate diagnostics measure the complete indexer path, not mismatched scoring buckets.",
        "supports_if": "All relevant ranks exercise the intended path; reference, graph and model-quality checks pass; complete-path time falls at matched inputs; and unprofiled paired intervals demonstrate useful TPOT or goodput improvement without unacceptable primary-workload or tail regressions. A long-context-only win supports only that scope, not deployment-wide promotion.",
        "rejects_if": "The feature already executes equivalently; required cache or shape contracts cannot be satisfied; numerical, causal or replay correctness fails without a credible repair; or adequately powered tests show no useful improvement over dense or the strongest eligible alternative. A native-workload regression rejects blanket activation even if a long-context diagnostic improves.",
        "inconclusive_if": "Only profiler-derived timings or streamed ITL improve; acceptance or prefix behavior cannot be joined to requests; eligible opportunity coverage is inadequate; the GPU correctness report is missing; or independent full-run intervals cannot distinguish benefit from regression.",
        "held_out_condition": "Previously unseen long-context lengths, single-request decode, ragged mixtures spanning short and long contexts, cold/warm prefixes, page-table remapping, preemption and mixed prefill/decode. Determine feasible H200 concurrency from actual KV residency; do not import H20 capacity.",
        "correctness": "Validate scores against an independent FP32 reference with justified tolerances, tie-aware selection against dense scoring, and a model-quality subset. Exercise invalid, duplicate and padded candidate handling; empty/partial contexts; request-local remapping; block64 layouts and strides; speculative causal bounds; and unchanged source-layer behavior. Capture short contexts and replay with changed lengths, pages and request assignments; compare eager results and check stable workspace allocation. Author-described tests are not evidence they passed on H200. Map to applicable G01-G05 when definitions are available.",
        "cost": "Higher integration and verification cost than plan sharing: complete kernel/dispatch review, numerical validation and three-arm comparison are required. Gate expensive long-context tests on eligibility and the unprofiled screen. Measure workspace and KV-capacity effects rather than infer them. Report P*T/(3600*N_output), with unknown full-node hourly price P; also report qualified-token cost. Profiled runs are excluded from the serving frontier."
      },
      "revision_reason": "Initial proposal incorporates the gather single-request regression and direct-scoring sample limitations by comparing alternatives within one hypothesis, retaining dense control and restricting any claim to demonstrated workloads."
    },
    {
      "id": "h200-attn-20261020-03",
      "parents": [],
      "operation": "generate",
      "statement": "Port or activate DeepSelect for eligible FP32 indexer top-k calls on SM90, only after checking the installed selector and extension build. The supplied vLLM patch adds a Hopper availability path and explicit dtype, width, k and alignment checks. Its value would come from faster selection over unchanged logits, independently of attention-head padding or candidate scoring. However, the DeepSelect library's headline H20 results concern small-batch BF16 inputs, while this integration requires FP32; a commenter also reports a competing radix advantage at k=2048. Therefore, compare against the fastest eligible existing vLLM backend chosen on calibration workloads, not merely torch.topk. Preserve existing fallbacks and isolate this selector change initially with dense scoring. Any later compact-logit combination needs separate confirmation because the remaining selection workload is different.",
      "observed_bottleneck": "No H200 top-k bottleneck is measured. The supplied installed sparse-scoring helper explicitly gates DeepSelect to capability family 100, but the installed selector resolver is absent from the excerpts. #59204 supplies integration code without performance results. DeepSelect #14 reports H20 BF16 microbenchmarks; FP32 serving gains are unknown. Its competing-radix commenter supplies different k/length regimes, with hardware, dtype and timing units unknown.",
      "mechanism": "Implementation evidence: #59204 adds SM90 availability and Hopper FP32 validation, plus input/output alignment checks and bounded-row selection support. Transfer inference: a faster selector can reduce time spent selecting the same top-k from unchanged scores. This does not create an SM90 sparse-scoring kernel. The library's BF16 cluster-performance claim does not establish the behavior or speed of this FP32 integration.",
      "proposed_change": "First inspect the installed indexer_topk resolver, actual selected backend, extension revision and SM90 build targets. If a useful delta exists, port the compatible #59204 selector integration and explicitly select DeepSelect only for validated inputs, retaining the best native fallback. Do not broaden sparse_mqa_logits.has_deep_select indiscriminately because its downstream sparse-scoring dependencies are separate.",
      "code_surface": "vllm/model_executor/layers/indexer_topk.py; vllm/config/kernel.py; cmake/external_projects/deepselect.cmake; relevant cache_utils integration and selector tests listed in #59204. Build and resolver changes are not fully visible in the supplied patch excerpt. The DeepSelect #14 kernel patch is unavailable in the supplied record.",
      "applicability": "Deferred pending rebase, compatible extension build, complete dispatch review and observed FP32 input contracts. Supplied checks require 0<k<=4096, width below 2^23, contiguous columns, a 128-byte-aligned input pointer and required input/output stride alignment. Actual k, width, row distribution and alignment are unknown. Compact candidate logits around 16K columns do not match #14's reported BF16 cluster regime starting at 128K.",
      "predicted_direction": "Potentially lower top-k latency and, if exposed, decode TPOT or cost per token. Gains may vanish or reverse for short rows, different k, larger row counts or already-competitive native kernels. H200 effect size is unknown.",
      "classification": "upstream_port",
      "alternatives": [
        {
          "explanation": "The current cooperative, persistent or per-row kernel is faster for the deployment's FP32 shapes.",
          "distinguishing_test": "Benchmark all eligible existing backends on observed inputs, choose the strongest static native comparator on calibration data, then freeze that choice before held-out tests. Include rows around the documented cooperative limit of 64."
        },
        {
          "explanation": "The apparent advantage comes from padding, layout copies, different end bounds or changed selection semantics.",
          "distinguishing_test": "Use identical logits and row bounds; include alignment conversion, allocation and dispatch in full-path timing. Check selected values and indices with explicit tie handling and downstream ordering requirements."
        },
        {
          "explanation": "Top-k improves in isolation but scoring, communication or scheduling dominates serving.",
          "distinguishing_test": "Keep scoring and other backends fixed, confirm selector activation and critical-path time separately, then require an independent unprofiled full-run improvement."
        }
      ],
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source_id": "github:vllm-project/vllm:59204:patch",
          "quote": "or current_platform.is_device_capability(90)",
          "relation": "supports"
        },
        {
          "source_id": "github:vllm-project/vllm:59204:patch",
          "quote": "or input.dtype == torch.float32",
          "relation": "context"
        },
        {
          "source_id": "code:h200-excerpts:attention",
          "quote": "and current_platform.is_device_capability_family(100)",
          "relation": "challenges"
        },
        {
          "source_id": "github:vllm-project/vllm:59204:live-page",
          "quote": "This pull request has merge conflicts",
          "relation": "challenges"
        },
        {
          "source_id": "github:deepseek-ai/DeepSelect:14:live-page",
          "quote": "Dispatch SM90 BF16 workloads",
          "relation": "context"
        },
        {
          "source_id": "github:deepseek-ai/DeepSelect:14:live-page",
          "quote": "though in top 2048, our previous algorithm is faster",
          "relation": "challenges"
        }
      ],
      "novelty": {
        "scientific": "Existing top-k backend integration; novelty is not a selection criterion.",
        "implementation": "Qualify the SM90 FP32 selector path on the pinned branch while keeping sparse-scoring architecture gates separate.",
        "workload": "Compare actual TP1 speculative row distributions and dense versus compact logits, rather than transferring BF16 library benchmarks.",
        "nearest_prior_art": "vLLM #59204 and DeepSelect #14; existing cooperative/persistent/per-row top-k.",
        "specific_delta": "Replace only eligible native selector calls with DeepSelect, conditional on absence and demonstrated advantage over a strong native comparator."
      },
      "prior_art_query": "SM90 FP32 indexer top-k",
      "experiment": {
        "control": "Supplied pinned baseline with dense scoring unchanged. Compare both deployed auto selection and the fastest eligible static native backend selected using disjoint calibration inputs. Do not use torch.topk as the sole performance comparator. Keep plan sharing and candidate-scoring changes out of the initial experiment.",
        "treatment": "Begin with source, build and configuration inspection. After a compatible port or activation, establish per-rank dispatch, pass correctness, screen unprofiled native agent-f75 and fixed-schedule Mooncake at seq64, then collect separate operator diagnostics. Confirm small serving gains with at least five alternating paired full-run blocks, baseline-drift checks and intervals based on full runs.",
        "metrics": "Activation: DeepSelect calls and rows divided by all eligible top-k calls and rows, with eligibility rejection reasons, dtype, k, width, alignment and row-count strata on every rank. Measure complete selection-path latency separately. Serving metrics include exact-token request TPOT, TTFT tails, throughput, historical-scorer goodput, replay lag, all-rank draft/verify/accepted deltas, KV blocks, preemption and graph fallback counts. Record missing counters and resets.",
        "supports_if": "The SM90 FP32 path demonstrably executes, preserves required selection semantics and model quality, beats the strongest native comparator including overhead on held-out shapes, and produces a useful paired serving improvement without unacceptable tail regression.",
        "rejects_if": "Equivalent eligible dispatch is already active; the necessary build or layout contracts cannot be met without erasing the benefit; correctness fails without a credible remedy; or adequately powered tests favor the best native selector or rule out useful serving improvement.",
        "inconclusive_if": "Only BF16 or torch.topk comparisons are available; extension architecture or selected dispatch is unverified; opportunities are insufficiently covered; or serving intervals remain wider than the predeclared useful effect.",
        "held_out_condition": "Unseen ragged and mixed batches, short and long contexts, cold/warm prefixes, speculative row counts below and above 64, and changing per-row end bounds. Test compact candidate logits only in a later isolated combination arm; do not add estimated gains from separate experiments.",
        "correctness": "Check independent reference values and tie-aware index sets, end<k padding, invalid/empty rows, supported k boundaries, input/output strides and alignment, and sorted-index semantics where consumed. Compare eager and graph replay with changing end tensors and request membership; verify allocation stability and fallback behavior. Run a model-quality subset because selection ordering or ties can affect downstream attention. Acceptance rate is diagnostic, not correctness. Map to applicable G01-G05 once defined.",
        "cost": "Moderate-to-high integration uncertainty because the PR needs rebasing and extension build compatibility is unresolved. Cheap source/build inspection and operator screening precede serving confirmation. Use unknown eight-GPU hourly price P and measured T/N_output for parameterized cost; include any layout-copy or workspace cost. Exclude profiled runs from the serving frontier."
      },
      "revision_reason": "Initial proposal narrows the claim to FP32 selector integration and replaces a weak torch.topk comparison with the strongest eligible existing vLLM backend."
    }
  ],
  "gaps": [
    "Three distinct mechanisms are retained; gather and direct paged scoring are competing arms of one hypothesis. All three remain deferred for deployment qualification, not measured H200 wins or asserted passes of the rubric threshold.",
    "Only supplied sources were assessed. No tools, retrieval, file changes, agents or experiments were used. The brief says 13 repositories but enumerates 16; the supplied artifacts do not establish repository-wide coverage.",
    "The pinned comparison is vLLM ac9126e58aa7bbab1856ba6593ba4d5003fea516 and serving checkout 11c249d28b2962f7384b4ab1fd7c1664704e7524 under the supplied image/model revision. Runtime inventory establishes configuration, not active kernels, per-rank load or measured performance. Partial imports and patch metadata do not establish complete integration.",
    "H200 dispatch, actual indexer shapes, compressed lengths, exposed bottlenecks, effect sizes and sustainable capacity remain unknown. Historical ranking claims and planning ranges were not used as measurements or selection priors. No H20 ITL result was converted into H200 TPOT.",
    "Small-head decode #59418 and prefill #61615/FlashMLA #26 do not supply the padding-removal mechanism for the unchanged TP1 64-attention-head baseline. DP4/EP4 does not create TP4/TP8 local head counts. Changing TP would require a separate deployment hypothesis.",
    "FlashMLA #200 is not retained: its V3.2 record compatibility and an overlap window are unestablished for this target, and the author reports pack-plus-attention without overlap at 0.740x. Matching 64 heads alone is insufficient.",
    "MISA's supplied experimental body is missing despite fulltext_available metadata. Its abstract cannot establish implementation, hardware, accuracy or deployment benefit, so it supports no selected hypothesis.",
    "The #62463 SM90 test execution report and model accuracy are unresolved; its tiny serving sample and unmatched profiling batches limit attribution. #59204's complete resolver/build integration and DeepSelect #14's kernel patch are unavailable here.",
    "G01-G05 definitions and historical scorer implementation are not supplied. Their exact mapping must be resolved before qualification. Production H200 SLOs and full-node price are unknown; the diagnostic 2s TTFT/50ms TPOT thresholds are not production requirements.",
    "Reported allgather_reducescatter dispatch, AIPerf environment compatibility and instrumented-profiler launch readiness remain unverified. They are prerequisites or attribution concerns, not additional optimization hypotheses supported by this evidence."
  ]
}
